1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
A mosquito lands on your arm.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,440
How many would it take to drain

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:04,400
all your blood?

4
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,080
A big swarm sounds like it could

5
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:06,560
do it.

6
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,000
But each bite is tiny.

7
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,360
Only females bite,

8
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:11,040
and each sips a drop smaller than

9
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,160
a grain of rice.

10
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:14,080
Your body holds about five litres of

11
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:14,640
blood,

12
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:15,920
roughly a big jug.

13
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:18,080
Fill that jug one tiny drop at

14
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:18,720
a time,

15
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,880
and you'd need about a million mosquitoes.

16
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,880
Real danger comes sooner:

17
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:25,280
after around four hundred thousand bites,

18
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:26,880
you'd lose enough blood to be in

19
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:27,920
serious trouble.

20
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:28,480
Luckily,

21
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,280
you'd swat,

22
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:31,040
scratch and run long before that.

23
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,640
So next time one bites you,

24
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:33,440
relax.

25
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:34,800
It's just one sip out of a

26
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:35,896
million.
